1
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:52,519
I always intended to give it
to the person I love most.

2
00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:55,520
<i>And now, I think I've found her.</i>

3
00:02:57,560 --> 00:02:59,800
Da, help me.

4
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:01,159
Win!

5
00:03:01,160 --> 00:03:02,519
Help me.

6
00:03:02,520 --> 00:03:04,319
Kang, Sarai,

7
00:03:04,320 --> 00:03:06,000
please forgive me.

8
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:33,680
The ketchup's here, Kang.

9
00:03:35,120 --> 00:03:36,280
Kang?

10
00:03:37,400 --> 00:03:38,400
Kang?

11
00:03:39,280 --> 00:03:41,920
- Kang?
- Where did Kang go?

12
00:03:42,840 --> 00:03:44,959
Maybe he's in the bathroom.

13
00:03:44,960 --> 00:03:46,760
Kang, ketchup's here.

14
00:03:49,040 --> 00:03:50,200
Kang.

15
00:03:52,280 --> 00:03:53,480
He isn't in the bathroom.

16
00:03:56,880 --> 00:03:59,800
- Kang.
- Kang.

17
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:02,120
He's not in the bedroom either.

18
00:04:12,520 --> 00:04:13,960
Where did he go?

19
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:26,000
Let me go. Let me go.

20
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:28,999
I can't believe

21
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,480
that this boy

22
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:33,480
is the child of Mr. Phum and Sarai.

23
00:04:36,120 --> 00:04:38,080
He looks exactly like your husband.

24
00:04:40,080 --> 00:04:42,880
Don't say it. I don't want to hear it.

25
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:47,400
Turns out

26
00:04:47,960 --> 00:04:50,640
the kid was right
under our noses all along.

27
00:04:51,440 --> 00:04:53,280
Thongdee really is clever.

28
00:04:54,760 --> 00:04:58,880
At last, I have a chance
to get revenge on them.

29
00:05:02,120 --> 00:05:03,320
What are you planning to do?

30
00:05:05,240 --> 00:05:07,519
We only took the kid
so we could demand a ransom

31
00:05:07,520 --> 00:05:11,320
and get money to fund our escape.

32
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:19,560
Stop here.

33
00:05:22,440 --> 00:05:23,560
Rewind the video a bit.

34
00:05:28,560 --> 00:05:29,960
That bastard.

35
00:05:32,080 --> 00:05:33,640
He's one of Sairung's men.

36
00:05:45,280 --> 00:05:48,200
Does Mr. Prawin
have any close friends elsewhere?

37
00:05:49,840 --> 00:05:54,360
Maybe he went on a guys' trip somewhere.

38
00:05:56,360 --> 00:06:00,360
I've already checked with everyone.
No one has seen him.

39
00:06:13,320 --> 00:06:14,400
Da.

40
00:06:15,920 --> 00:06:17,400
Help me, Da.

41
00:06:18,800 --> 00:06:21,160
Da, help me.

42
00:06:21,920 --> 00:06:23,200
Hm?

43
00:06:26,080 --> 00:06:27,360
What's wrong, Da?

44
00:06:28,840 --> 00:06:29,880
The island...

45
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:32,800
The island where I saw Win in my dream.

46
00:06:35,160 --> 00:06:36,680
What about it?

47
00:06:38,720 --> 00:06:40,399
It was Skull Island.

48
00:06:40,400 --> 00:06:41,680
What?

49
00:07:31,480 --> 00:07:32,920
Why is it so hot?

50
00:07:39,920 --> 00:07:42,160
No matter how many times you try,

51
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:48,120
you can't leave this island.

52
00:07:54,080 --> 00:07:56,840
Why did my life have to end like this?

53
00:07:58,360 --> 00:07:59,920
I don't want to die.

54
00:08:00,440 --> 00:08:02,200
I don't want to die.

55
00:08:03,080 --> 00:08:05,040
I don't deserve to die.

56
00:08:14,320 --> 00:08:15,840
That's impossible, Da.

57
00:08:16,360 --> 00:08:19,680
There's no reason
for Win to go to Skull Island.

58
00:08:22,040 --> 00:08:23,480
Kaimook's right.

59
00:08:25,360 --> 00:08:26,439
Besides,

60
00:08:26,440 --> 00:08:29,199
the police have restricted access

61
00:08:29,200 --> 00:08:31,320
to that island
ever since the last incident.

62
00:08:32,400 --> 00:08:35,640
Nobody can go there.

63
00:08:40,080 --> 00:08:41,159
Da,

64
00:08:42,360 --> 00:08:44,559
most islands look pretty much the same.

65
00:08:44,560 --> 00:08:46,320
I think you're just overthinking it.

66
00:08:47,120 --> 00:08:48,799
But I'm sure

67
00:08:48,800 --> 00:08:53,240
the island I saw in my dream
was definitely Skull Island.

68
00:08:55,080 --> 00:08:57,399
Then tell me this.

69
00:08:57,400 --> 00:08:59,799
Why would Win go to Skull Island

70
00:08:59,800 --> 00:09:02,080
when he knows it's haunted?

71
00:09:04,560 --> 00:09:07,160
I've never told Win about the island.

72
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:12,400
But I don't think

73
00:09:13,520 --> 00:09:16,080
Mr. Prawin would go to Skull Island.

74
00:09:17,560 --> 00:09:19,080
Especially if he went with Ms. Pat,

75
00:09:19,840 --> 00:09:23,880
they'd probably choose
some beautiful tourist island,

76
00:09:24,720 --> 00:09:27,160
not a terrifying place like Skull Island.

77
00:10:19,400 --> 00:10:21,640
Win. Win.

78
00:10:23,440 --> 00:10:24,400
Win.

79
00:10:24,920 --> 00:10:26,240
Stop!

80
00:10:37,680 --> 00:10:39,640
How many times have I told you

81
00:10:40,880 --> 00:10:43,040
not to mess with these two spirits?

82
00:10:47,600 --> 00:10:49,080
Do you want to try me?

83
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:00,320
Wait.

84
00:11:05,840 --> 00:11:07,680
We're dead.

85
00:11:08,800 --> 00:11:10,640
But why can't
our spirits leave this island?

86
00:11:23,800 --> 00:11:25,520
He's gone.

87
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:27,800
Damn it!

88
00:11:29,160 --> 00:11:31,280
I don't want to stay
on this island anymore.

89
00:11:34,280 --> 00:11:35,360
Da!

90
00:11:36,200 --> 00:11:38,119
Can you hear me, Da?

91
00:11:38,120 --> 00:11:40,320
Help me get off this island, Da.

92
00:11:41,360 --> 00:11:43,400
- Da!
- Who's Da?

93
00:11:44,880 --> 00:11:46,200
My sister.

94
00:11:46,720 --> 00:11:49,960
She has a sixth sense.
If we keep trying to contact her,

95
00:11:50,480 --> 00:11:52,400
maybe she'll sense something

96
00:11:53,840 --> 00:11:57,480
Da, can you hear me?

97
00:11:58,640 --> 00:12:01,000
Help me get off this island, Da.

98
00:12:02,840 --> 00:12:03,840
<i>- Da!</i>
- No!

99
00:12:04,600 --> 00:12:05,880
What's wrong, Da?

100
00:12:07,760 --> 00:12:09,079
Na.

101
00:12:09,080 --> 00:12:11,440
When did I fall asleep?

102
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:16,559
Right after we got back.
You said you were hungry,

103
00:12:16,560 --> 00:12:18,879
so I was going to make
something simple for you to eat.

104
00:12:18,880 --> 00:12:21,520
Before I realized,
you were already fast asleep.

105
00:12:24,240 --> 00:12:26,919
I guess
I didn't sleep very well last night.

106
00:12:26,920 --> 00:12:28,640
That's why I'm this sleepy.

107
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:34,920
I heard you cry out.
Did you have another nightmare?

108
00:12:35,480 --> 00:12:38,080
I saw Win again.

109
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:45,760
I think you're so worried about Win
that it's showing up in your dreams.

110
00:12:47,920 --> 00:12:50,319
But I really have
a bad feeling about this.

111
00:12:50,320 --> 00:12:52,559
I'm sure something terrible
has happened to Win.

112
00:12:52,560 --> 00:12:55,960
That's why he's trying
to reach out to me and ask for help.

113
00:12:57,880 --> 00:12:59,640
Then what are you going to do?

114
00:13:02,440 --> 00:13:03,959
I'm going to Skull Island.

115
00:13:03,960 --> 00:13:05,040
What?

116
00:13:06,400 --> 00:13:10,400
That ghost may have imprisoned him,
just like what happened to Mook.

117
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:14,000
But that's extremely dangerous, Da.

118
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:16,799
I have the sacred thread
from Venerable Sir.

119
00:13:16,800 --> 00:13:19,960
I believe it will protect me.

120
00:13:24,200 --> 00:13:27,040
Then I'm going with you.

121
00:13:30,400 --> 00:13:31,640
Na...

122
00:13:37,160 --> 00:13:39,720
Thank you for not abandoning me.

123
00:13:44,680 --> 00:13:46,880
I promise I will never abandon you.

124
00:13:47,720 --> 00:13:50,000
No matter whether we end up
facing humans or ghosts.

125
00:14:00,320 --> 00:14:01,240
Come here.

126
00:14:02,640 --> 00:14:03,840
Stay quiet.

127
00:14:07,560 --> 00:14:09,840
How much are you planning
to demand from your husband?

128
00:14:11,320 --> 00:14:12,799
Fifty million.

129
00:14:12,800 --> 00:14:14,640
Fifty million?

130
00:14:15,240 --> 00:14:16,680
That's not much

131
00:14:17,280 --> 00:14:20,000
for the child he deliberately
brought into this world...

132
00:14:21,600 --> 00:14:24,560
and compensation for the child I lost.

133
00:14:37,320 --> 00:14:38,280
Hey.

134
00:14:39,080 --> 00:14:40,000
Listen carefully.

135
00:14:41,080 --> 00:14:44,920
If you try to make enough noise
for someone to hear...

136
00:14:51,960 --> 00:14:54,000
the first person to die

137
00:14:56,680 --> 00:14:58,600
will be your Venerable Sir.

138
00:14:59,160 --> 00:15:00,319
Understand?

139
00:15:00,320 --> 00:15:01,760
Yes.

140
00:15:03,880 --> 00:15:06,880
Good. You're easy to talk to.

141
00:15:10,560 --> 00:15:14,320
Anyway, when are you
going to contact your husband?

142
00:15:32,440 --> 00:15:33,600
Mr. Phum,

143
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:36,720
are you really just
going to sit here and wait?

144
00:15:37,880 --> 00:15:39,160
Calm down.

145
00:15:39,680 --> 00:15:42,040
Sairung will contact us eventually.

146
00:15:45,520 --> 00:15:48,920
I really don't understand
why she would take Kang.

147
00:15:51,600 --> 00:15:53,480
There's only one thing that woman wants.

148
00:16:02,120 --> 00:16:04,400
<i>You must be very worried, Mr. Phum.</i>

149
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:09,640
Tell me what you want. Stop wasting time.

150
00:16:11,120 --> 00:16:12,439
I knew

151
00:16:12,440 --> 00:16:15,839
someone as smart as you
would understand immediately.

152
00:16:15,840 --> 00:16:17,320
Let's get straight to the point.

153
00:16:18,680 --> 00:16:21,480
I want 50 million baht in cash.

154
00:16:24,800 --> 00:16:26,160
Tell me where to bring it.

155
00:16:29,880 --> 00:16:32,400
Behind the cemetery at Wat Tai.
Seven o'clock tonight.

156
00:16:33,680 --> 00:16:34,880
Wat Tai?

157
00:16:35,480 --> 00:16:36,640
Fine.

158
00:16:38,200 --> 00:16:39,640
Don't try anything clever.

159
00:16:40,160 --> 00:16:42,280
If you do,

160
00:16:42,800 --> 00:16:44,880
not only will that temple boy die,

161
00:16:45,640 --> 00:16:49,000
you'll never see your son again.

162
00:16:51,480 --> 00:16:52,480
What?

163
00:16:53,680 --> 00:16:55,920
My son with Sarai is with you?

164
00:16:58,600 --> 00:17:00,880
Sairung? Sairung?

165
00:17:05,839 --> 00:17:07,318
<i>The number you're trying to call
is not available.</i>

166
00:17:07,319 --> 00:17:09,880
- Damn it.
- Mr. Phum,

167
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:13,040
our son is still alive?

168
00:17:13,920 --> 00:17:15,079
It seems so.

169
00:17:18,240 --> 00:17:20,359
Will she hurt him?

170
00:17:23,359 --> 00:17:24,400
Don't worry.

171
00:17:25,119 --> 00:17:27,520
I'll bring our son back.

172
00:17:37,080 --> 00:17:39,520
How was it? Your husband agreed to pay?

173
00:17:40,120 --> 00:17:42,240
I told you he would.

174
00:17:45,720 --> 00:17:46,799
Great.

175
00:17:46,800 --> 00:17:50,040
I never imagined this kid
would be worth 50 million baht.

176
00:17:56,040 --> 00:17:57,239
Sir,

177
00:17:57,240 --> 00:17:59,039
I'm begging you.

178
00:17:59,040 --> 00:18:01,040
Please let me take care of Venerable Sir.

179
00:18:01,640 --> 00:18:04,079
He looks very sick.

180
00:18:04,080 --> 00:18:07,120
I promise I won't make any noise.

181
00:18:07,720 --> 00:18:09,960
Please.

182
00:18:10,480 --> 00:18:13,440
Please. Can I?

183
00:18:16,200 --> 00:18:17,480
I think

184
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:20,440
maybe we should
let him take care of Thongdee.

185
00:18:21,160 --> 00:18:24,560
If he dies right now, we'll be in trouble.

186
00:18:29,240 --> 00:18:30,279
Fine.

187
00:18:30,280 --> 00:18:31,640
Thank you.

188
00:19:21,320 --> 00:19:23,320
I think you should wait for me here.

189
00:19:23,840 --> 00:19:25,399
Please let me come with you.

190
00:19:25,400 --> 00:19:29,279
It's too dangerous. Someone like Sairung
definitely has something planned.

191
00:19:29,280 --> 00:19:32,119
That's exactly why I need to go.

192
00:19:32,120 --> 00:19:35,680
Did you forget I'm already dead?

193
00:19:36,400 --> 00:19:39,639
If Sairung decides to play dirty,
I can help you.

194
00:19:39,640 --> 00:19:43,240
Please. Let me go help save our son.

195
00:19:46,360 --> 00:19:48,559
Alright. But you have to promise me

196
00:19:48,560 --> 00:19:51,520
that you won't let anyone know
you're living inside Pakarang's body.

197
00:19:52,120 --> 00:19:54,319
And don't hurt anyone
unless it's necessary.

198
00:19:54,320 --> 00:19:56,480
I don't want you creating more bad karma.

199
00:19:57,280 --> 00:19:58,720
I promise.

200
00:20:15,880 --> 00:20:19,200
Don't look back. Don't look back.

201
00:20:19,800 --> 00:20:23,360
Who says karma doesn't exist?
I don't believe them.

202
00:20:26,080 --> 00:20:27,480
I agree.

203
00:20:29,320 --> 00:20:31,680
The reason Sompong
ended up insane like this

204
00:20:33,200 --> 00:20:36,120
is because of what he did to Sarai.

205
00:20:38,960 --> 00:20:41,600
Then what are you
going to do about Sompong?

206
00:20:43,040 --> 00:20:46,160
I'll have to let my dad decide.

207
00:20:50,200 --> 00:20:53,840
But for now, the doctors
should keep treating him as best they can.

208
00:20:55,080 --> 00:20:56,960
We already brought him here, after all.

209
00:20:58,120 --> 00:21:01,840
Don't look back. Look forward.

210
00:21:05,040 --> 00:21:06,480
Thank you so much

211
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:11,160
for helping with all this
from the beginning.

212
00:21:12,440 --> 00:21:13,280
But

213
00:21:14,040 --> 00:21:17,040
I'll still have to trouble you
to keep helping for now.

214
00:21:17,840 --> 00:21:20,280
My dad and I

215
00:21:21,360 --> 00:21:25,240
need to find my missing brother first.

216
00:21:26,880 --> 00:21:28,000
No problem, my friend.

217
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:38,960
It's here! It's here!

218
00:21:39,880 --> 00:21:41,920
There!

219
00:21:48,920 --> 00:21:49,840
Are you done yet?

220
00:21:50,720 --> 00:21:51,720
Yes.

221
00:21:53,200 --> 00:21:55,000
Don't even think about running.

222
00:21:57,720 --> 00:22:00,040
- Let's go.
- What about your men?

223
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:02,280
We'll meet them there.

224
00:22:02,880 --> 00:22:04,480
They'll definitely come, right?

225
00:22:06,040 --> 00:22:09,120
Don't worry.
I've used them for a long time.

226
00:22:09,640 --> 00:22:12,720
As long as there's money,
everything's taken care of.

227
00:22:48,320 --> 00:22:49,400
Sairung.

228
00:22:52,960 --> 00:22:54,040
Sairung.

229
00:22:57,040 --> 00:22:58,080
Sairung.

230
00:22:58,840 --> 00:23:00,040
I'm here.

231
00:23:17,360 --> 00:23:19,800
- Be careful.
- Okay.

232
00:23:21,440 --> 00:23:22,520
How brave.

233
00:23:23,120 --> 00:23:25,639
You want to be
a rich man's mistress so badly

234
00:23:25,640 --> 00:23:27,360
you're not even afraid of death.

235
00:23:28,440 --> 00:23:30,679
Kang has nothing to do with this.

236
00:23:30,680 --> 00:23:32,000
Let him go.

237
00:23:32,520 --> 00:23:35,719
Oh, what a heroine.

238
00:23:35,720 --> 00:23:37,240
Acting like you love children.

239
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:40,480
And what business do you have here,
butting in like this?

240
00:23:41,680 --> 00:23:42,520
This is

241
00:23:43,400 --> 00:23:46,120
between husband and wife.

242
00:23:47,280 --> 00:23:49,040
But since you came,

243
00:23:49,640 --> 00:23:52,400
I'll kindly give you something fun to do.

244
00:24:02,040 --> 00:24:04,080
- Go over there first.
- Okay.

245
00:24:06,200 --> 00:24:07,440
Go get her.

246
00:24:44,400 --> 00:24:45,480
Kang.

247
00:24:46,400 --> 00:24:47,440
Venerable Sir...

248
00:24:49,440 --> 00:24:50,800
Venerable Sir...

249
00:25:05,440 --> 00:25:06,840
Venerable Sir, you're awake.

250
00:25:09,160 --> 00:25:11,640
Why are you here?

251
00:25:12,160 --> 00:25:13,600
What happened?

252
00:25:14,120 --> 00:25:16,480
Well...

253
00:25:32,640 --> 00:25:33,920
Go get the money bag.

254
00:25:54,160 --> 00:25:55,560
I can't believe

255
00:25:56,240 --> 00:25:57,880
a man like you

256
00:25:58,400 --> 00:26:01,200
would come without a single bodyguard.

257
00:26:02,560 --> 00:26:05,240
You got the money. Let Kang and my son go.

258
00:26:07,040 --> 00:26:08,839
You really are a fool.

259
00:26:08,840 --> 00:26:12,239
You don't even recognize
your own flesh and blood.

260
00:26:12,240 --> 00:26:13,880
What are you talking about?

261
00:26:22,120 --> 00:26:24,640
Do whatever you want with that woman.

262
00:26:25,560 --> 00:26:26,799
Let's go, Pong.

263
00:26:26,800 --> 00:26:30,039
Let the man
watch his concubine's love scene

264
00:26:30,040 --> 00:26:32,560
to pass the time.

265
00:26:33,880 --> 00:26:35,960
Goodbye, my dearest Mr. Phum.

266
00:26:36,760 --> 00:26:38,640
I hope you have fun.

267
00:26:41,600 --> 00:26:43,120
Let Kang and my son go!

268
00:26:43,880 --> 00:26:44,719
Sairung!

269
00:26:44,720 --> 00:26:46,840
Let Kang and my son go!

270
00:26:55,960 --> 00:26:59,360
You're so pretty. I'll take you to heaven.

271
00:27:06,040 --> 00:27:07,720
She's hot.

272
00:27:40,360 --> 00:27:42,320
Sarai.

273
00:27:42,920 --> 00:27:43,839
Sarai, don't.

274
00:27:43,840 --> 00:27:44,920
Please.

275
00:27:48,080 --> 00:27:52,200
I'm leaving! I'm out!

276
00:27:52,800 --> 00:27:53,880
Yes.

277
00:27:54,440 --> 00:27:57,560
These aren't the ones who deserve to die.

278
00:28:13,200 --> 00:28:15,880
By now, Mr. Phum must be
so furious he's coughing blood,

279
00:28:16,520 --> 00:28:20,280
watching Pakarang get taken
by those men right in front of him.

280
00:28:22,040 --> 00:28:24,000
How satisfying.

281
00:28:25,760 --> 00:28:27,560
Give me back my son.

282
00:28:31,960 --> 00:28:32,920
Sarai.

283
00:28:39,040 --> 00:28:41,080
Pong! Help me!

284
00:28:41,800 --> 00:28:43,120
Where is my son?

285
00:28:53,720 --> 00:28:54,840
You bastard!

286
00:29:15,440 --> 00:29:17,240
I give up! I give up!

287
00:29:19,200 --> 00:29:20,479
Where is my son?

288
00:29:20,480 --> 00:29:22,239
Tell me now!

289
00:29:22,240 --> 00:29:23,920
I'll tell you. Let me go first.

290
00:29:26,840 --> 00:29:28,720
Where's my son?

291
00:29:29,240 --> 00:29:30,359
I give up. Wait.

292
00:29:30,360 --> 00:29:31,920
- I give up.
- Tell me.

293
00:29:46,760 --> 00:29:48,160
You coward dog!

294
00:29:57,680 --> 00:30:00,000
I don't know. I don't know anything.

295
00:30:01,080 --> 00:30:04,039
Please don't hurt me.

296
00:30:04,040 --> 00:30:05,200
You must die.

297
00:30:05,800 --> 00:30:07,440
I'm scared.

298
00:30:08,320 --> 00:30:10,560
<i>Don't create more bad karma.</i>

299
00:30:19,680 --> 00:30:20,680
Venerable Sir?

300
00:30:29,920 --> 00:30:32,120
Every life follows its karma.

301
00:30:33,080 --> 00:30:35,080
Let Sairung go.

302
00:30:36,120 --> 00:30:37,160
In the end,

303
00:30:37,760 --> 00:30:40,480
she will have to face
the karma she created.

304
00:30:41,920 --> 00:30:42,919
But...

305
00:30:42,920 --> 00:30:45,360
I mean well.

306
00:30:46,240 --> 00:30:47,480
Believe me.

307
00:30:48,560 --> 00:30:51,000
Don't create more hatred and bad karma.

308
00:30:52,280 --> 00:30:54,800
Your child is safe now.

309
00:30:56,840 --> 00:30:59,800
My child? Where is my child?

310
00:31:09,240 --> 00:31:11,520
Sarai. Sarai.

311
00:31:12,040 --> 00:31:12,879
Mr. Phum.

312
00:31:12,880 --> 00:31:15,520
How are you?

313
00:31:16,120 --> 00:31:19,000
Mr. Phum. I know now.

314
00:31:19,520 --> 00:31:21,120
I know where our child is now.

315
00:31:22,520 --> 00:31:23,800
Where is he?

316
00:31:32,680 --> 00:31:34,320
Mr. Thongdee

317
00:31:34,960 --> 00:31:37,360
is going to take us to our son.

318
00:31:38,880 --> 00:31:39,920
Yes.

319
00:31:46,760 --> 00:31:47,800
Venerable Sir.

320
00:31:52,480 --> 00:31:54,039
- Kang.
- Mr. Phum.

321
00:31:54,040 --> 00:31:55,039
Ma'am.

322
00:31:55,040 --> 00:31:56,559
- Kang.
- Kang, are you alright?

323
00:31:56,560 --> 00:31:58,280
I'm alright.

324
00:32:00,880 --> 00:32:03,240
Thank goodness they didn't hurt you.

325
00:32:05,520 --> 00:32:07,040
And where is my son?

326
00:32:08,400 --> 00:32:10,160
He's right in front of you.

327
00:32:20,080 --> 00:32:21,720
Kang is your son.

328
00:32:25,640 --> 00:32:28,480
I was the one who took Kang
from Sarai's house

329
00:32:29,240 --> 00:32:30,840
and raised him until he grew up.

330
00:32:31,880 --> 00:32:35,400
The only thing Kang had with him
was the Buddha amulet necklace

331
00:32:35,920 --> 00:32:38,240
that he wears.

332
00:33:18,080 --> 00:33:19,840
That's your necklace, Sarai.

333
00:33:23,560 --> 00:33:24,560
Yes.

334
00:33:27,040 --> 00:33:29,000
I put this necklace on my son

335
00:33:29,720 --> 00:33:31,880
when he was born.

336
00:33:32,400 --> 00:33:35,040
Oh, my child.

337
00:33:35,600 --> 00:33:36,720
My child.

338
00:33:59,000 --> 00:34:02,120
Am I really your son, Mr. Phum, ma'am?

339
00:34:06,040 --> 00:34:08,320
From now on, call me Dad,

340
00:34:09,480 --> 00:34:11,320
and call her Mom.

341
00:34:16,520 --> 00:34:19,760
Yes, Dad, Mom.

342
00:34:20,520 --> 00:34:23,760
I'm so happy I finally found you two.

343
00:34:25,600 --> 00:34:26,840
My child.

344
00:34:53,719 --> 00:34:58,399
Your hair is long now. I'll take you
to get your haircut when we get home.

345
00:34:58,400 --> 00:34:59,400
Okay.

346
00:35:12,560 --> 00:35:15,080
I'll take good care of you, Kang.

347
00:35:27,120 --> 00:35:28,040
Sarai.

348
00:35:30,680 --> 00:35:32,280
Yes, Venerable Sir?

349
00:35:35,080 --> 00:35:37,000
Don't call me that anymore.

350
00:35:40,040 --> 00:35:43,079
I still keep calling him
Venerable Sir too.

351
00:35:43,080 --> 00:35:45,520
Then what should I call him?

352
00:35:53,200 --> 00:35:55,440
Call him Uncle Thongdee.

353
00:35:56,040 --> 00:35:57,199
You know what?

354
00:35:57,200 --> 00:36:00,560
Uncle Thongdee has done
a great kindness for me.

355
00:36:14,880 --> 00:36:17,280
Thank you, Thongdee.

356
00:36:21,920 --> 00:36:23,600
There's something I need to tell you.

357
00:36:25,720 --> 00:36:26,960
What is it?

358
00:36:28,760 --> 00:36:32,000
My past, before I became a monk.

359
00:36:34,440 --> 00:36:37,719
Thongdee, no matter

360
00:36:37,720 --> 00:36:39,040
who you used to be

361
00:36:39,800 --> 00:36:41,480
or what you did,

362
00:36:42,080 --> 00:36:43,560
I don't care.

363
00:36:46,360 --> 00:36:47,720
But I...

364
00:36:49,440 --> 00:36:51,280
- I am...
- My wife, my child,

365
00:36:52,480 --> 00:36:53,640
let's go home.

366
00:36:56,120 --> 00:36:56,960
Kang,

367
00:36:57,560 --> 00:36:59,280
say goodbye to Uncle Thongdee.

368
00:37:02,840 --> 00:37:04,199
Venerable...

369
00:37:04,200 --> 00:37:06,840
I mean, Uncle Thongdee, I'm going now.

370
00:37:12,320 --> 00:37:14,160
I'm sorry, Kang,

371
00:37:16,040 --> 00:37:18,280
for making you struggle for so many years.

372
00:37:19,480 --> 00:37:21,960
I'm happy I got to live with you.

373
00:37:22,480 --> 00:37:24,440
I'll come visit often.

374
00:37:26,360 --> 00:37:27,640
Good luck.

375
00:37:31,760 --> 00:37:32,720
Let's go.

376
00:37:33,240 --> 00:37:34,720
I'll get going now.

377
00:37:36,000 --> 00:37:37,040
Let's go.

378
00:37:37,920 --> 00:37:38,960
Go wait in the car.

379
00:37:44,400 --> 00:37:47,279
A small gesture from me,

380
00:37:47,280 --> 00:37:50,039
as thanks for raising Kang
until he grew up.

381
00:37:50,040 --> 00:37:52,280
I can't accept this.

382
00:37:53,720 --> 00:37:54,760
Don't think of Kang

383
00:37:55,280 --> 00:37:57,600
as a favor.

384
00:37:58,880 --> 00:38:02,439
It was something I should have done.

385
00:38:02,440 --> 00:38:04,720
Please take it. I insist.

386
00:38:06,160 --> 00:38:07,120
You should go home.

387
00:38:11,640 --> 00:38:12,800
Thank you.

388
00:38:50,280 --> 00:38:51,600
Kang, are you hungry?

389
00:38:54,360 --> 00:38:56,400
Our son is asleep.

390
00:38:58,160 --> 00:39:00,280
He must be exhausted.

391
00:39:02,400 --> 00:39:05,520
Mr. Phum, did you really
give money to Thongdee?

392
00:39:06,560 --> 00:39:07,920
I did. But he refused to take it.

393
00:39:08,440 --> 00:39:10,160
He's a really good man.

394
00:39:12,080 --> 00:39:14,639
Thongdee has done so much for me.

395
00:39:14,640 --> 00:39:16,879
Even when I was a wandering spirit,

396
00:39:16,880 --> 00:39:19,079
he helped me many times.

397
00:39:19,080 --> 00:39:23,160
He always dedicated merit to me
even if we never knew each other before.

398
00:39:25,480 --> 00:39:28,719
Actually, when I first saw him as a monk,
he looked familiar.

399
00:39:28,720 --> 00:39:31,919
After he left the monkhood,
he seemed even more familiar.

400
00:39:31,920 --> 00:39:34,200
I just can't remember
where I've seen him before.

401
00:39:37,000 --> 00:39:40,880
Actually, his voice sounds familiar too.

402
00:39:41,640 --> 00:39:45,960
But I can't remember where I heard it.

403
00:39:55,560 --> 00:39:58,799
Forget it. If we can't remember,
then there's no point forcing it.

404
00:39:58,800 --> 00:40:01,919
All that matters is that
he is a benefactor to our family.

405
00:40:01,920 --> 00:40:03,440
Without him,

406
00:40:04,040 --> 00:40:06,400
we would never have reunited.

407
00:40:16,080 --> 00:40:18,720
We're screwed. A boat's coming.

408
00:40:19,840 --> 00:40:21,919
- Help me! Help me!
- Hey!

409
00:40:21,920 --> 00:40:23,760
- Where are you going?!
- Help me!

410
00:40:57,960 --> 00:40:59,160
I'm glad

411
00:40:59,920 --> 00:41:02,120
you finally know the truth.

412
00:41:07,800 --> 00:41:09,120
You bastard.

413
00:41:17,360 --> 00:41:19,320
Why aren't you begging for your life?

414
00:41:26,920 --> 00:41:28,040
Begging?

415
00:41:29,240 --> 00:41:30,880
I've been waiting for this moment.

416
00:41:31,760 --> 00:41:35,280
Waiting for the chance
to pay with my life. Why would I beg?

417
00:41:39,440 --> 00:41:40,520
You think talking like this

418
00:41:41,120 --> 00:41:43,080
is going to make me forgive you?

419
00:41:45,240 --> 00:41:46,360
I know.

420
00:41:47,320 --> 00:41:50,719
I know your spirit suffered

421
00:41:50,720 --> 00:41:53,320
in that coral forest beneath the sea.

422
00:41:54,240 --> 00:41:55,480
Me too.

423
00:41:56,000 --> 00:41:58,080
I've been suffering.

424
00:41:58,600 --> 00:42:02,039
Raising Kang all these years
felt like carrying hell inside my heart.

425
00:42:02,040 --> 00:42:03,160
Liar!

426
00:42:05,280 --> 00:42:06,480
Go ahead, Sarai.

427
00:42:07,400 --> 00:42:08,640
Kill me.

428
00:42:09,520 --> 00:42:10,920
I'm ready.

429
00:42:13,000 --> 00:42:15,200
I will kill you, you monster.

430
00:42:15,800 --> 00:42:17,560
Raising my son

431
00:42:18,400 --> 00:42:21,320
doesn't erase what you did to me.

432
00:42:39,720 --> 00:42:41,519
I'm going to take you somewhere.

433
00:42:41,520 --> 00:42:43,199
- Where?
- Skull Island.

434
00:42:43,200 --> 00:42:44,239
What?

435
00:42:44,240 --> 00:42:47,600
Win... is dead.

436
00:42:50,000 --> 00:42:52,560
You're quite brave
to come back here again.

437
00:42:53,360 --> 00:42:55,320
Our substitute has arrived.

438
00:42:58,000 --> 00:42:59,679
If we want to leave this island,

439
00:42:59,680 --> 00:43:01,200
we have to kill her.

440
00:43:34,240 --> 00:43:36,480
Subtitle translation by: Panuwat Baikeawon
